  "id": "COMPOUND:16867 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Funtumine may be a potential inhibitor of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Funtumine to DNA polymerase iota, which is subsequently targeted by a compound with the structure described, and this compound in turn targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The second pathway connects Funtumine to CD276 antigen, which is targeted by 6-O-Veratroylcatalpol, which also targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The third pathway links Funtumine to DNA polymerase iota, which is targeted by CID 53630653, which also targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These findings collectively indicate that Funtumine may interact with components of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through different molecular mechanisms, possibly by modulating the activity of enzymes involved in DNA replication or by targeting downstream components of the complex. The evidence is consistent with the possibility that Funtumine could act as a modulator of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this relationship.",
